      "id": "assertion-message-matches",
      "kind": "noul",
      "ask": "When this check fails, its message ($MSG) tells the reader something untrue about what was wrong, judged against the condition ($COND) that was actually tested.",
      "note": "The check fires when the guard is true for if-throw shapes and when the condition is false for assert and invariant shapes; judge the message against the case in which it is shown. Only the condition and the message are compared; whether the check itself is correct is not the question. A throw inside a test double is not a check on the program's state and is out of scope, whether or not the double has a name; in a test file, a throw whose condition is a call count, a route or an input value and whose message is a failure being simulated is one. A nested guard is judged as one check whose condition is the outer and inner conditions combined.",
